[SIZE=5][B]📦 Supported Versions[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Spigot:[/B] 1.17 – 26.3
[*][B]Paper:[/B] 1.17 – 26.3
[*][B]Purpur:[/B] 1.17 – 26.3
[*][B]Folia:[/B] 1.19.4 – 26.3
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]📄 Installation[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Download the jar (the same file works on every server and version above)
[*]Put it in your server's [FONT=Courier New]plugins[/FONT] folder
[*]Restart the server
[/LIST]
Only the server needs it. Players don't install anything.

[SIZE=5][B]⚙️ Configuration[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Turn each message on or off, and require permissions, in [FONT=Courier New]config.yml[/FONT].
[*]Change the messages in the [B]translation files[/B] ([FONT=Courier New]translations/<lang>.yml[/FONT]) using [URL='https://docs.papermc.io/adventure/minimessage/format/']MiniMessage[/URL]. Placeholders: [FONT=Courier New]%amount%[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]%durability%[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]%max%[/FONT].
[*]Run [FONT=Courier New]/ged reload[/FONT] after changing anything.
[/LIST]

[SPOILER="📝 config.yml"]
[CODE=yaml]# Configuration version, DO NOT MODIFY THIS VALUE!
config-version: 3.0.0

######################################################
#                     Language                       #
######################################################

# Language setting (available: en_US, es_ES, de_DE, fr_FR, zh_CN, ja_JP, th_TH)
# If the specified language file is missing, it will fall back to en_US.
lang: en_US

# Adding custom language
# 1. Create a new file in the translations directory
# 2. Use en_US.yml as a template
# 3. Modify the file as needed
# 4. Set language to your custom language file name

######################################################
#                    Permissions                     #
######################################################

# When set to true, players require permissions to see any message.
# This setting applies globally to all message types.
# See below for a list of permissions.
require-permission: false

# Permissions for displaying messages:
#
#  gainexpdisplay.gainexp - Display text when gaining experience
#  gainexpdisplay.mending - Display text when repairing items with Mending

######################################################
#                      Settings                      #
######################################################

# When set to true, players will see text when gaining exp.
gain-xp:
  enabled: true

# When set to true, players will see text when repairing items with Mending.
mending-repair:
  enabled: true[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[SIZE=5][B]📚 Commands & Permissions[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][FONT=Courier New]/ged reload[/FONT] ([FONT=Courier New]gainexpdisplay.reload[/FONT], operators): reload the config and messages
[*][FONT=Courier New]gainexpdisplay.gainexp[/FONT] (everyone): see the XP message, when [FONT=Courier New]require-permission[/FONT] is [FONT=Courier New]true[/FONT]
[*][FONT=Courier New]gainexpdisplay.mending[/FONT] (everyone): see the Mending message, when [FONT=Courier New]require-permission[/FONT] is [FONT=Courier New]true[/FONT]
[/LIST]

[SPOILER="❓ FAQ"]
[B]Does it work on Spigot?[/B]
Yes, from 2.2.0. Paper, Purpur and Folia work too.

[B]I'm updating from an older version. Do I lose my settings?[/B]
No. Old config files are updated automatically, your settings and messages are kept, and a backup is saved in [FONT=Courier New]plugins/GainExpDisplay/backup/[/FONT].

[B]Can I hide the messages for some players?[/B]
Set [FONT=Courier New]require-permission: true[/FONT] and take away [FONT=Courier New]gainexpdisplay.gainexp[/FONT] or [FONT=Courier New]gainexpdisplay.mending[/FONT] with a permissions plugin like LuckPerms.
[/SPOILER]

